From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Blake <chrisrblake93@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 10:34:44 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 08/15] mb/radxa/x4: Match the devicetree to the board

Correct the devicetree against the v1.11 schematic and the stock V007
firmware.

PCIe and GPIO:
- The M.2 Wi-Fi card is an RTL8852BE on lane PCIE4, root port 4
  (8086:54bb). Move it from pcie_rp1 to pcie_rp4; clock source and
  CLKREQ 2 stay.
- Disable ASPM on all three root ports, as the stock firmware does.
- Enable LTR on all three root ports and mark root port 9 built-in,
  as the stock firmware does. The M.2 slot is not hot-pluggable.
- Route GPE0 DW0/1/2 to GPP_A, GPP_R and GPD, as the stock firmware
  does (PMC GPIO_CFG 0x432).

USB:
- J4 has two USB3 Type-A ports (USB2 1 + USB3 1, USB2 2 + USB3 2). J5
  has one USB3 Type-A port (USB2 3 + USB3 3) and one USB 2.0 Type-A
  port (USB2 5). USB2 6 is the RP2040, USB2 7 the RTL8852BE's
  Bluetooth. Disable USB2 4 and 8, which have no net, and USB3 4, whose
  lane is PCIE4.
- Add _UPC/_PLD for the wired ports, with one PLD group per connector
  so the OS pairs each USB3 port with its USB2 port.
- USB2_PORT_MID matches the stock PHY settings, and the stock firmware
  applies no USB3 tuning. The OC pins are only pulled up, so OC_SKIP
  stays.
- Turn off the TCSS xHCI: TCP0 is unused and TCP1 drives an HDMI port.

Display:
- J3 is on DDI B (HPD GPP_A18, DDC GPP_H15/H17), and J2 on Type-C PHY 2
  (lanes TCP1) as a fixed HDMI output (HPD GPP_A20, DDC GPP_E20/E21).
  Enable HPD/DDC on DDI B and DDI port 2 instead of DDI A, which is not
  wired.
- Leave DdiPortAConfig and DdiPortBConfig at 0: 1 means eDP in this
  FSP. Disable both pad buffers on GPP_E20/E21, as the stock firmware
  does.
- The old data.vbt has HDMI on DDI A and DP on DDI B, so the FSP GOP
  lights neither port. Replace it with a VBT that has the stock child
  devices, in the BDB 256 layout this FSP's GOP needs.

CPU: enable EIST, and set the N100's power limits to PL1 13 W, PL2
25 W and PL4 78 W. PL1 is 13 W instead of the 6 W TDP, which caps
sustained clocks.

eMMC: enable HS400. Without emmc_enable_hs400_mode, FSP clears the
HS400 capability and edk2's SdMmcPciHcDxe picks HS200, which needs
tuning and has no fallback on Intel hosts. With HS400 advertised it
uses HS400 Enhanced Strobe, which needs no tuning.

Console: set UART0 (test pads TP1/TP2) to PchSerialIoSkipInit. With
PchSerialIoPci, FSP-S initialises the controller again while coreboot
keeps printing to the BAR it programmed.

Audio: enable HDA SDI 0, the line the ALC269Q answers on. coreboot
passes pch_hda_sdi_enable to FSP as is, so without it FSP turns the
lane off and only the HDMI codec is found. Reset the codec's audio
function and write the five Realtek coefficients the stock firmware
writes, so the codec starts in the same state.

TPM: declare Intel PTT as a drivers/crb device, so coreboot writes the
\_SB.TPM ACPI device (MSFT0101) that the OS binds its TPM driver to.
The TPM2 table alone is not enough.

ISH: turn it off. No sensors are wired to it, and the stock pad table
leaves its pads' buffers off, so the OS driver only times out waiting
for its firmware.

